.TH FOXSSH 1 "2026" "Fox SSH" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
foxssh \- system-wide SSH tunnel VPN client (GUI and command line)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B foxssh
.br
.B foxssh --hidden
.br
.B foxssh
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without arguments foxssh opens the graphical client. With a command it works headless and does what the GUI does:
connect/disconnect, profile management, DNS, Iran bypass, logs. All system traffic goes through the SSH tunnel;
Iranian destinations go direct.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "connect [" NAME "] [profile options]"
Connect. NAME is a profile name or id; without it the default profile is used.
.B --host
without NAME connects once without saving. Options:
.BR --no-wait ", " -q ", " --timeout " SEC, " --dns1 " IP, " --dns2 " IP, " --bypass ", " --no-bypass .
.TP
.B disconnect
Disconnect (aliases: down, stop).
.TP
.B status " [" --json ]
Show state. Exit status 0 if connected, 3 otherwise.
.TP
.B logs " [" -n " N] [" -f ]
Show the engine log; \-f follows.
.TP
.B list, show NAME, add, edit NAME, remove NAME, select NAME, import FILE
Manage profiles.
.TP
.B dns [D1 [D2]]
Show or set DNS servers used inside the tunnel.
.TP
.B bypass [on|off|list|add X|remove X]
Iran bypass. X is an IP, CIDR or domain.
.TP
.B lang [fa|en]
Language of engine messages.
.TP
.B update-list, forget-keys
Update the Iran IP list; forget saved SSH host keys.
.TP
.B service enable [NAME] | disable | start | stop | restart | status
Control foxssh-auto.service, which connects at boot using a profile from /etc/foxssh.
.SH PROFILE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --name " NAME" ", " --host " HOST" ", " -p,\ --port " PORT" ", " -u,\ --user " USER" ", " --udpgw " PORT"
.TP
.BR --pass " PW, " --pass-file " FILE, " --pass-stdin ", " --ask-pass
Password sources (prefer a file or stdin; --pass is visible in ps). FOXSSH_PASS is used when nothing else is given.
.TP
.BI -L " SRC:HOST:PORT" ", " -R " SRC:HOST:PORT" ", " -D " PORT"
Local, remote and dynamic (SOCKS) forwards; repeatable. On edit they are added to the existing ones.
.TP
.BR --any-local ", " --any-remote ", " --no-any-local ", " --no-any-remote
Listen on 0.0.0.0 instead of 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.B --clear-tunnels
(edit) drop existing forwards first.
.SH SCOPE
.TP
.B --system
Use /etc/foxssh. This is the default when run as root. Commands that need root re-run themselves through pkexec.
.TP
.B --no-system
Use ~/.config/foxssh (the same store as the GUI). Default for normal users.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/foxssh/foxssh.conf
Settings: selected (default profile id), dns1, dns2, bypass (true/false), manual (semicolon separated), lang.
.TP
.I /etc/foxssh/profiles.d/*.conf
One profile per file (mode 600, root only). Keys:
name, host, port, user, pass, udpgw, local, remote, dynamic (comma separated, e.g. local=8080:intranet:80,9090:db:5432),
anyLocal, anyRemote. The file name without .conf is the profile id.
.TP
.I ~/.config/foxssh/settings.properties
User-scope profiles and settings.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
foxssh add --name work --host example.com -u me --ask-pass -D 1080
foxssh connect work
sudo foxssh add --name office --host vpn.example.com -u me --pass-file /root/pw
sudo foxssh service enable office
.fi
